---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import DisplayFontPreload from '../../components/page/DisplayFontPreload.astro';
import PageHead from '../../components/page/PageHead.astro';
import PageLayout from '../../components/page/PageLayout.astro';

const personSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Person",
  "name": "Marius Gehler",
  "url": "https://boatpass.de/en/about/",
  "jobTitle": "Founder & Developer",
  "image": "https://boatpass.de/ueber-uns-hero.webp",
  "worksFor": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "BoatPass",
    "url": "https://boatpass.de",
  },
  "description": "Marius Gehler is the founder and developer of BoatPass – the modern study app for the German boating license (SBF Binnen & See).",
  "knowsAbout": [
    "Sportbootführerschein",
    "SBF Binnen",
    "SBF See",
    "Android development",
    "iOS development",
    "ELWIS question catalog",
  ],
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Boatpass – the Story Behind the SBF App"
  description="Who is behind Boatpass? The story and motivation behind the German boating license study app – built by one developer who sat the exam himself."
  lang="en"
  altUrl="https://boatpass.de/ueber-uns/"
>
  <DisplayFontPreload slot="head" />
  <script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(personSchema)} />
  <!-- Seitenkopf und schmale Spalte (Spec Runde 3, 3.1/3.5) -->
  <PageHead
    lang="en"
    eyebrow="About us"
    lede="The person behind the app – and why it exists."
    cta
  >
    About BoatPass
  </PageHead>

  <PageLayout variant="narrow">

    <!-- Author profile -->
    <div class="pg-card pg-card--legal pg-portrait">
      <img
        src="/ueber-uns-hero.webp"
        alt="Marius Gehler, founder of BoatPass, at the helm of a motorboat in a marina"
        width="1000"
        height="1250"
        loading="eager"
        fetchpriority="high"
      />
      <div class="pg-portrait-body">
        <p class="pg-card-title pg-card-title--lg">Marius Gehler</p>
        <p class="pg-card-label">Founder & Developer of BoatPass</p>
        <p class="pg-p">
          Hi, I'm Marius – founder and developer of BoatPass. I've been building apps for years, and
          I built BoatPass with one clear goal: a boating-license app that feels genuinely good on your
          phone – fast, clean and motivating.
        </p>
        <div class="pg-pills">
          {["SBF Binnen", "SBF See", "ELWIS catalog", "Android & iOS"].map(tag => (
            <span class="pg-pill">{tag}</span>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Card: Why BoatPass exists -->
    <div class="pg-card pg-card--legal">
      <h2 class="pg-card-label">Why BoatPass exists</h2>
      <img
        src="/ueber-uns.webp"
        alt="Marius Gehler at the helm of a sailboat on the water"
        width="1000"
        height="750"
        loading="lazy"
        class="pg-card-img"
      />
      <p class="pg-p pg-p--sm">
        When I started studying, I asked friends who already had their license. Their verdict was almost
        always the same: there are apps with good content – but none that make studying on your phone
        actually enjoyable. Clunky menus, uninspired interfaces, questions you just memorize by rote.
      </p>
      <p class="pg-p pg-p--sm">
        That stuck with me. I've been building apps in my spare time for years – BoatPass is my passion
        project alongside my day job. So I built the app I wish I'd had: one that makes studying on your
        phone genuinely enjoyable – and that maps 1:1 onto the official question catalog.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Card: What matters to me -->
    <div class="pg-card pg-card--legal">
      <h2 class="pg-card-label">What matters to me</h2>
      <p class="pg-p pg-p--sm">
        Studying theory for the boating license shouldn't feel like a chore. You should enjoy learning and
        make fast progress. That's why every question comes with clear explanations and memory aids –
        instead of just „right/wrong“. The material sticks, and you get out on the water sooner.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Card: Where the content comes from -->
    <div class="pg-card pg-card--legal">
      <h2 class="pg-card-label">Where the content comes from</h2>
      <p class="pg-p pg-p--sm">
        The questions and answers in BoatPass are not my invention: they come 1:1 from the official
        question catalog published by the German Federal Ministry for Digital and Transport via
        <a href="https://www.elwis.de/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="pg-inline-link">ELWIS</a>.
        Which catalog and which revision sits behind each licence is listed on the licence pages, with a
        direct link so you can check it against the official source yourself.
      </p>
      <p class="pg-p pg-p--sm">
        The explanations and memory aids I write myself – based on the catalog and the underlying
        regulations (BinSchStrO, SeeSchStrO, COLREGs). BoatPass is developed independently and is not
        affiliated with DSV, DMYV or any public authority.
      </p>
      <p class="pg-p pg-p--sm">
        If you spot a mistake in an explanation, tell me. I check every report myself and correct it in
        the next update.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Card: My promise -->
    <div class="pg-card pg-card--legal">
      <h2 class="pg-card-label">My promise</h2>
      <ul class="pg-checks">
        <li class="pg-check">
          <span class="pg-check-mark">✓</span>
          Always up-to-date official question catalog (ELWIS)
        </li>
        <li class="pg-check">
          <span class="pg-check-mark">✓</span>
          No subscription – buy once, use it for good
        </li>
        <li class="pg-check">
          <span class="pg-check-mark">✓</span>
          Explanations & memory aids instead of rote memorization
        </li>
        <li class="pg-check">
          <span class="pg-check-mark">✓</span>
          Built by a developer who takes design seriously
        </li>
        <li class="pg-check">
          <span class="pg-check-mark">✓</span>
          Report a mistake – I check every report myself and fix it in the next update
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Card: Contact -->
    <div class="pg-card pg-card--legal">
      <h2 class="pg-card-label">Contact</h2>
      <p class="pg-p pg-p--sm">
        Feedback, found a bug, or just a question? Reach me via the
        <a href="/en/contact/" class="pg-inline-link">contact form</a> –
        I read every message myself.
      </p>
    </div>

  </PageLayout>
</BaseLayout>
